UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Arthritis pain can arise from joints, surrounding tissues and the nervous system, with inflammatory and degenerative types behaving differently. The guide says structured movement, anti-inflammatory eating, weight management, heat or cold, and good sleep can help. Start small, track pain and function weekly, and seek GP or physiotherapist advice for swollen red joints, weight loss, prolonged stiffness, numbness or weakness.' WHERE slug='swimming-full-body-arthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The post says arthritis-related spinal or joint pain should be managed by identifying inflammatory or degenerative patterns. It presents structured movement and graded exercise as first-line, supported by diet, weight management, heat or cold, sleep routines and small weekly goals. It advises GP or physiotherapy review for hot swollen joints, weight loss, prolonged morning stiffness, numbness or weakness.' WHERE slug='expert-qa-spinal-injections-vs-exercise';
