UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The guide explains that knee osteoarthritis pain can involve cartilage, fluid, ligaments, muscle and the nervous system, and that management depends on symptom patterns. It recommends graded movement, anti-inflammatory eating, weight management, heat or cold, sleep hygiene, and small weekly tracking goals. It advises seeking GP or physiotherapy help for hot swollen joints, weight loss, prolonged stiffness, numbness or weakness.' WHERE slug='straight-leg-raises-knee-osteoarthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The post explains that a strong PIP application for arthritis should focus on how symptoms affect daily living and mobility, not just the diagnosis. It advises tracking symptoms, describing good and bad days, linking pain to specific tasks, gathering clinical evidence, avoiding blank sections, starting early, and speaking to a GP or rheumatology team when symptoms or support needs change.' WHERE slug='pip-for-arthritis-how-to-build-a-strong-application';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The post explains how people with arthritis can prepare for a Universal Credit Work Capability Assessment by giving an honest picture of symptoms, including bad days, and bringing medical evidence, therapy notes, medication details and a symptom diary. It highlights personalised clinical, occupational and workplace support, advises prompt clinician contact if symptoms worsen, and notes decisions can be challenged.' WHERE slug='universal-credit-and-arthritis-limited-capability-for-work';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Disabled Students’ Allowance can help students with arthritis access tailored university support, including specialist equipment, non-medical helpers and academic adjustments. The article advises applying early, contacting disability services, tracking symptoms, maintaining gentle movement and self-care, and involving support networks. It also recommends speaking to a GP, physiotherapist or rheumatologist if symptoms worsen or affect study.' WHERE slug='university-with-arthritis-disability-support-and-dsa';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Choosing a career with arthritis means considering energy demands, posture and adaptability rather than seeking one ideal job. The article recommends personalised clinical advice, symptom tracking, gentle regular movement, ergonomic changes, flexible working and regular breaks. It warns against ignoring symptoms or delaying adjustments, and advises prompt review for new swelling, fever, worsening function or work-related pain.' WHERE slug='expert-qa-choosing-a-career-friendly-to-arthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Reasonable adjustments for arthritis work best when tailored to your symptoms and job, combining ergonomic equipment, task changes, flexible hours or home working, and a supportive workplace. The article advises early, open communication with employers, regular review as needs change, symptom tracking, and clinician input, especially for new swelling, worsening pain, reduced function, poor sleep, mood changes or stress.' WHERE slug='reasonable-adjustments-that-actually-help';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Children do not usually inherit arthritis in a simple, direct way. Some types, including rheumatoid and psoriatic arthritis, have a genetic component, so a close relative can slightly raise susceptibility, but most children will not develop it. Genes interact with triggers such as lifestyle, infections and environment. Seek medical advice for persistent joint symptoms.' WHERE slug='expert-qa-will-my-children-inherit-my-arthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The article advises honest, age-appropriate conversations with children about arthritis, giving simple reassurance to younger children and more detail to older ones. It says clear communication can reduce worry and support family coping. Avoid hiding the condition, overwhelming medical detail, blame or false promises; invite questions and seek clinical advice for worsening symptoms, new concerns or overwhelm.' WHERE slug='talking-to-children-about-your-arthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The post says partners can support someone with arthritis through small daily acts, open communication and practical help with joint-straining tasks. It stresses clinician-led, personalised care combining medication, regular comfortable movement, symptom tracking and lifestyle support. It advises pacing, not stopping prescribed treatment, avoiding quick fixes, and seeking prompt review for swelling, fever, severe pain or rapid loss of function.' WHERE slug='supporting-a-partner-with-arthritis-a-practical-handbook';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Asking for help with arthritis is framed as a strength and part of self-management, not a personal failing. The post advises personalised clinical input, symptom tracking, gentle regular movement, accepting practical support and making specific requests. It warns against minimising symptoms or waiting for crisis, and recommends prompt review for swelling, fever, rapid functional loss, side effects or emotional distress.' WHERE slug='expert-qa-how-to-ask-for-help-without-feeling-guilty';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Biologics for inflammatory arthritis are considered under UK guidance, usually when conventional DMARDs have not worked adequately, with DAS28 helping assess disease activity and guide treat-to-target decisions. Evidence from trials and reviews supports earlier targeted therapy for slowing joint damage and improving quality of life, while regular monitoring helps manage infection risk, side effects and treatment response.' WHERE slug='nhs-access-to-biologics-how-the-approval-pathway-works';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The article says private rheumatology may offer faster specialist appointments and scans, but diagnosis can still require several visits and tests, and costs are usually ongoing. It stresses evidence-based arthritis care: early diagnosis, appropriate medication, gentle movement, lifestyle and psychological support, symptom tracking, and prompt clinical advice for new swelling, fever, severe pain or worsening function.' WHERE slug='private-rheumatology-in-the-uk-when-its-worth-considering';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='During an arthritis flare-up, the article advises adapting rather than stopping exercise: keep gentle, regular, low-impact movement within comfort, track symptoms, and avoid pushing through sharp pain or increasing activity too quickly. It says guidance and reviews support combined medication, movement and lifestyle support, while new swelling, fever, rapid functional loss or severe symptoms need clinician review.' WHERE slug='expert-qa-exercising-through-a-flare-up';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Sustained remission in rheumatoid arthritis means stable minimal or no disease activity, not a cure. The article says it is a key treatment goal, often maintained through ongoing medication, monitoring, gentle regular movement and lifestyle support. It advises personalised clinician guidance, symptom tracking, pacing activity, and prompt review for swelling, fever, rapid function loss or medication side effects.' WHERE slug='what-sustained-remission-means-in-ra';